# Travel Documents and Entry Requirements

## Passenger Responsibility

Passengers are responsible for ensuring that they possess all documents
required for their complete journey, including transit points.

SkyDesk provides general booking assistance but does not make final
immigration or entry decisions. Requirements can change at short notice.

## Passports and Identity Documents

The required identity document depends on nationality, destination,
transit countries, and applicable agreements.

A passport may need to remain valid for a minimum period after the
planned travel date. Some destinations also require empty passport
pages.

Customers should verify requirements with official government or
consular sources before travelling.

## Name on the Booking

The passenger name should match the travel document used for the
journey.

Minor formatting differences, such as spaces or title fields, are not
necessarily problems, but spelling errors should be reported as soon as
possible.

A ticket cannot normally be transferred to another person by changing
the passenger name.

## Visas

Visa requirements depend on factors including:

-   passenger nationality;
-   destination;
-   purpose of travel;
-   length of stay;
-   transit airports;
-   residence permits or existing visas.

Possessing a flight ticket does not guarantee eligibility to enter or
transit a country.

## Transit Requirements

A passenger may require a transit visa even when they do not intend to
leave the airport.

Self-transfer itineraries can require the passenger to pass immigration,
collect baggage, and enter the transit country before checking in again.

Customers should pay particular attention to transit requirements when
travelling on separate tickets.

## Electronic Travel Authorizations

Some destinations require an electronic authorization before departure
even when a traditional visa is not required.

Approval should be obtained before travelling according to the
destination authority's rules.

## Children and Minors

Children require their own valid travel documents where applicable.
Additional parental consent documents may be required when a minor
travels alone, with one parent, or with someone who is not a legal
guardian.

## Document Checks

Airlines may verify passports, visas, residence permits, or other
documents during online check-in, at the airport, or before boarding.

A passenger can be denied boarding if required documents are missing or
invalid.

## Entry Requirement Changes

Entry, health, and immigration requirements can change after a booking
is made. Customers should recheck official requirements shortly before
departure.

SkyDesk cannot guarantee the accuracy of third-party or previously
retrieved immigration information.

## Support Limitations

SkyDesk support can help customers find booking details, airline
information, and general guidance contained in the knowledge base.

Support must not guarantee that a particular visa, passport, permit, or
document will be accepted by an airline or border authority.
